    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d124">

                <pb facs="0177" n="85" xml:id="pg85"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Hopkins Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Harriman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Presidents
                        Special Assistant</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hopkins</hi>)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d124-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">routine</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-11-12">12 November 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Personal and secret for Hopkins from Harriman.</p>
                <p>Since cabling the President last night<anchor n="2" xml:id="d124-f2"/> about our
                    joining him at Cairo on the 22nd I have been wondering whether it would not be
                    of value for us to make our reports prior to the meeting with Molotov. We have
                    of course considerable information both military and political of reactions to
                    and developments since the Conference broke up which perhaps should be discussed
                        beforehand.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d124-f3"/></p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d124-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d124-f1-content">
                <p>Sent by the United States Naval Attaché, Moscow, via Navy channels.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d124-f2" n="2" xml:id="d124-f2-content">
                <p>Telegram of November 12, 1943, <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref
                        target="#pg80">p. 80</ref>.</p>
            </note>
